[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m, next to a placeholder "Example task" label. I haven't opened it in a browser yet.

  - [1mThe checkbox:[0m it's a standard browser [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m inside a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so clicking the text also toggles
    it, and it works with the keyboard and screen readers.
  - [1mThe on/off state:[0m this is the checkbox's own checked state. A small script adds a [38;5;153mdone[39m class to the task when it's
    checked, and that greys out and strikes through the text.
  - [1mAdding more tasks:[0m copy the [38;5;153m<label class="task">…</label>[39m block and change the text. Every checkbox gets the same
    behavior without extra wiring.

  The checked state isn't saved, so it resets when the page reloads. I can save it in the browser with [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m if
  you want. I haven't committed anything.

